2248-### 7l-1. (HIGH) SHIP A FIX WHOSE DETECTOR PROVABLY CANNOT DISCRIMINATE IT?  *(the `hold_question`)*
2249-
2250-Four seats reached this independently, by different routes:
2251-
2252-| seat | how it put the wall |
2253-|---|---|
2254-| grok | *"the witness address is not a type-1 tag, and empty-slot data cannot pin the extract"* |
2255-| glm | it *"conflates IMPLEMENT with explicit-all-ones DECLINE, silent with latched, and can false-pass on stale all-ones unless the destination register is pre-seeded"* |
2256-| minimax, kimi(sub) | only a **populated bus-1 device** could separate them |
2257-
2258-**An empty bus 1 answers all-ones whether the model implements type-1 or merely fakes the reply**,
2259-and nothing in this tree places a device on bus 1. So:
2260-
2261-> **(a)** ship the fix and DISCLOSE the non-discriminating detector under clause (e); or
2262-> **(b)** ADD a synthetic bus-1 device to the apparatus so the row becomes possible.
2263->
2264-> **(b) is an addition to the test apparatus made in order to observe a fix** ??? which is precisely
2265-> the shape the addition licence exists to police, and it is not obviously refused by it either,
2266-> since the licence governs PRODUCT additions. **That boundary is the question.**
2267-
2268-*glm's pre-seeding point is the one improvement available under (a) and should be taken either way:
2269-seed the destination register so a stale all-ones cannot false-pass.*
